,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":true,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106048","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106048","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106048.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106048.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"<!--\r\nPlease target the `master` branch in priority.\r\n\r\nRelevant fixes are cherry-picked for stable branches as needed by maintainers.\r\n\r\nTo speed up the contribution process and avoid CI errors, please set up pre-commit hooks locally:\r\nhttps://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/contributing/development/code_style_guidelines.html\r\n-->\r\n\r\nRequires #77937 to be merged first\r\n\r\nThis PR adds the option to generate CollisionShapes without being restricted to a specific physics body type when importing a scene.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4d65038d-8477-4097-83fe-23e5eb739f10\r\n\r\nLayer and Mask options are hidden from the inspector when using Collision Only, as those will be determined by the parent body used later.\r\n\r\nThis will allow reusing the same imported CollisionShapes in both static and dynamic contexts, as you can just instance the same scene.\r\n\r\nCurrently, you would have to generate the CollisionShapes manually for different usages of the imported scene, and if you make changes to the imported scene meshes, the CollisionShapes will not reflect those changes, and you will need to regenerate them manually again.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106048/reactions","total_count":10,"+1":5,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":2,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":3},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106048/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}